// Regression fixture for issue #630, the decisive case: a procedure whose
// bare *return* type is a scalar needing an import. `Uint8List`/`Decimal`
// appear only in the generated `Future<...>` signatures — no data class,
// no field, anywhere in the schema, carries either type. An
// implementation that scans procedure args and procedure-owned `type`
// fields (the obvious reading of #630) still fails this fixture; only one
// that also scans `procedure.return_type` passes it.
//
// `Keep` exists so the schema has a model; it uses neither scalar.

model Keep {
  id Int @id
  name String
}

procedure fetchBlob(): Bytes
procedure fetchTotal(): Decimal
